# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file the context is ~5 GB — .git alone is 4.1 GB, runs/ 594 MB,
# storage/ 285 MB, models/ 109 MB — and every `docker compose build` uploads all
# of it to the daemon before the first instruction runs.
#
# One entry here is a correctness fix rather than a speed one:
# dashboard/node_modules. The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and THEN `COPY dashboard/`,
# so an un-ignored node_modules from the host overwrites the freshly installed
# one — and this repo is developed on Windows, so it carries
# lightningcss-win32-x64-msvc and the win32 rolldown binding. Those cannot load
# in node:22-slim, and the failure is a build error deep inside vite rather than
# anything naming the real cause.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Version control and tooling metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Python: the image installs from requirements.txt, and a host venv is the wrong
# platform anyway.
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
htmlcov
.coverage

# Node: reinstalled inside the image (see the header). dist is rebuilt there too,
# so shipping the host's would mask a build that no longer works.
dashboard/node_modules
dashboard/dist

# Secrets. Not copied by the Dockerfile — compose passes .env at RUN time via
# env_file — so it has no business entering the context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime and per-deployment data. All three are bind-mounted by
# docker-compose.yml, never baked in.
storage
test_storage
models

# Research artefacts: training runs, datasets, exports. Large and irrelevant to
# a server image.
runs
datasets
files

# Not copied by the Dockerfile (it takes app/, migrations/ and dashboard/ only).
# NOTE: this is root-anchored, so dashboard/scripts is untouched — the prebuild
# hook there copies MapLibre's worker into public/, and without it every vector
# source silently fails to load.
scripts
tests
docs
*.md

# Compose itself never needs to be in the image.
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
